        },
        {
            "id": "of07",
            "hsla": "hsla(331.55,95.38%,83.89%,0.780)",
            "description": "The Balinese live on the island of Bali, in the archipelago country of Indonesia. They speak a language (also called Balinese) which, together with their religion, reflects a Malayo-Polynesian culture influenced by Buddhism and Hinduism. Balinese culture is renowned for its fascinating arts including dance, drama, sculpture and handcrafts. Traditional subsistence focused on wet-rice farming regulated by temple-based irrigation societies. The island has become an important tourist destination in recent years.",
