            "id": "fa08",
            "hsla": "hsla(65.27,95.43%,83.47%,0.770)",
            "description": "The Bambara are a Mande-speaking people located mostly in Mali, West Africa. They live in nucleated village communities and most Bambara earn their living cultivating a variety of crops and raising domesticated animals. Many augment their income by participating in a variety of non-agricultural activities including trade, wage labor, and small-scale craft production.",
            "highest_bt": "Africa",
            "bt": "Western Africa",
