            "id": "am04",
            "hsla": "hsla(331.55,95.31%,85.65%,0.810)",
            "description": "Cambodians are mostly from the Khmer ethnic group, who comprise about 90 percent of the population of the country of Cambodia. The designation \u201cCambodia\u201d refers to a Westernized transliterations of Kambuja, a Sanskrit name used by an ancient Khmer civilization that reached a peak during the Angkor period (802-1432) when Khmer kings built Angkor Wat and ruled an irrigation-based empire extending beyond the boundaries of the present-day nation of Cambodia. Most Khmer are small landholders, with rice as their main crop, supplemented by gardens, fishing, and earning money in a variety of side pursuits.",
