            "hsla": "hsla(331.55,95.29%,83.89%,0.780)",
            "description": "The Central Thai live in central and southern Thailand and speak a dialect of the Thai language of the Tai-Kadai family.  The original home of the Thai people was in the Chinese province of Yunnan from where they migrated south in successive waves, beginning about AD 1050. Wet-rice agriculture dominates the economy with about four-fifths of the population living in rural communities. The kingdom of Thailand was never colonized by a Western nation. Practicing Theravada Buddhism, most of Thai men have been ordained as priests, although only a small minority makes the priesthood their life work.",
