            "id": "sp09",
            "hsla": "hsla(355.37,95.28%,83.10%,0.760)",
            "description": "The Karaj\u00e1 are found on or near the island of Bananal on the middle Rio Araguaia, in central Brazil. Settlements consist of houses strung along rivers, and subsistence is based primarily on fishing, supplemented by shifting horticulture, hunting, and gathering. There is some participation in the market economy through commercial fishing, cattle herding, and handicrafts for sale to tourists, especially weaving. Dual descent emphasizes the matriline, although patrilineal moieties determine inheritance of ceremonial roles and chieftainship.",
