            "id": "om06",
            "hsla": "hsla(242.29,95.31%,84.37%,0.790)",
            "description": "&#x22;Manus&#x22; refers to residents of the Papua New Guinea province of Manus. Manus Province includes the main island of Manus (an island 272 km north-northeast of the mainland of Papua New Guinea) and offshore islands. The Manus language family contains scores of distinct languages; although many people know several Manus languages much of the communication between groups is in Melanesian pidgin. Sociopolitical life is organized on the village and patriclan level.",
