        {
            "id": "ox06",
            "hsla": "hsla(242.33,95.21%,84.37%,0.790)",
            "description": "The Marquesans are the inhabitants of the six larger islands of the Marquesan Island group: Nukuhiva, 'Ua Pou, 'Ua Huka, Fatuiva, Tahuate, and Hora Oa, including intermittent occupation of some of the smaller islands of the group (e.g. Eiao). There has also been a large scale emigration of Marquesans to Tahiti. Subsistence is based on tree products (e.g. breadfruit, bananas, plantains) and root-crop horticulture supplemented by fishing. The political organization of the Marquesas consists of a number of chiefdoms, each without clearly defined territorial domains. Social organization was hierarchical, based on \"tapu\" principles, ritual occupation, sex, age, chiefly rank and property ownership.",
            "highest_bt": "Oceania",
