            "id": "am35",
            "hsla": "hsla(331.55,95.31%,78.84%,0.800)",
            "description": "The Rhade are one of the Chamic-speaking ethnic minority peoples living in the Darlac plateau of Vietnam. Their traditional economy relied on the cultivation of rice on rain-fed upland swidden plots. The basic building block of society was the longhouse group, consisting of matrilineally-related women and their in-marrying spouses, as well as children born of the marriage. A cluster of longhouses formed largely self-governing villages. Following Vietnam\u2019s independence from French colonial rule, villages were increasingly absorbed into the national political and administrative system.",
