            "id": "ss18",
            "hsla": "hsla(355.21,95.26%,80.92%,0.770)",
            "description": "The Warao Indians, fishermen and incipient agriculturalists, inhabit the Orinoco Delta of northeastern Venezuela and adjacent areas.  All Warao speak mutually intelligible variants of the same language. Warao has traditionally been considered an isolate, without affiliation with one of the great South American language families.",
